{
 "item": "11",
 "title": "Micropolar cavity: centre lines against the finite-difference solution, fields, the slab cut",
 "status": "final",
 "caption": "Lid-driven cavity filled with the micropolar fluid: K = 3, Reynolds number 400 on mu_inf (1,000 on mu), l = L / 20 (25 dx at n = 500, 12.5 dx at n = 250), Theta = l^2, w = 0 on the four walls, Ma = 0.01, thesis configuration with the default walls. (a) u on the vertical centre line and (b) v on the horizontal centre line, time means over the last 20 L / U (MLS samples at 1,001 points, every 25th shown): the micropolar run (circles; crosses: n = 250) and the same fluid by finite differences (dotted); solid and dashed: Newtonian runs on the same particles with the viscosities mu_inf (Reynolds number 400) and mu + kappa (Reynolds number 250). (c) Micro-rotation and (d) micro-rotation minus half the curl of the velocity at the last step of run `mp_n500_k2` (two slabs, 5090 + XTX; dashed line: the cut); the second vanishes in the core and marks the wall layers of thickness l. Colour scales end at the 99.5th percentile of the magnitude. Runs: `newtonian_re400_n500`, `newtonian_re250_n500`, `mp_n500`, `mp_n250`, `mp_n500_k2`; tag `thesis-ch5-rc2`. The check of the case is the dotted line and table 11b: the same equations solved by finite differences on the host (stream function, vorticity and micro-rotation on a uniform grid, second order, steady state; grids of 128, 192, 256 intervals, extrema extrapolated to zero spacing). Extrema (u_min, v_max, v_min) of the micropolar fluid: particle run -0.3580, 0.3228, -0.4627 U, finite differences -0.3567, 0.3213, -0.4614 U; the particle run is stronger by +0.3, +0.5, +0.3 %, and its centre lines differ from the finite-difference ones by 2.1e-03 (u) and 1.6e-03 (v) U rms. The two Newtonian runs against their finite-difference solutions: +0.7, +0.9, +0.7 % (mu_inf), +0.4, +0.6, +0.4 % (mu + kappa). Table 11b also lists finite-difference variants of the micropolar case (other lengths l, no spin inertia, walls that do not hold w, w held on the lid only or on the walls at rest only). Table 11c: the traction of the lid on the micropolar fluid over that on the Newtonian fluid of viscosity mu_inf, minus one, is 0.296, 0.232, 0.144, 0.077 at l = L / 10, 20, 40, 80, against delta / lambda = 0.597, 0.299, 0.149, 0.075, where lambda = mu_inf U / traction = 0.063 L is the shear length of the lid in that Newtonian fluid (finite differences; both tractions on the same grid, 256 intervals, 384 for l = L / 80): the first-order rule with the shear length in the place of the gap, within 3 % from l = L / 40 down. The run at n = 250 minus the run at n = 500: rms difference of the centre lines 3.0e-03 (u) and 3.5e-03 (v) U, extrema -5.3e-03, +5.0e-03, -6.1e-03 U (standard error of the time means 2e-05). Two slabs minus one slab: rms difference of the centre lines 2.1e-05 (u) and 1.6e-05 (v) U, extrema -5.2e-06, +1.4e-05, -2.1e-06 U (standard error of the time means 1e-05).",
